IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: Part 5 Division 4A -- the electronic register of members kept by the Registrar
-- (ss 196A to 196E). Layer 1: the law, objectively. Part sgm. Text: the SSO informal consolidation as the file renders it (a rendering, not the official text).
--
-- The Registrar keeps the register of members of a private company (s 196A); a company incorporated before 3 January 2016 had to lodge its
-- information (s 196B), must keep its old registers for 7 years (s 196D), and ss 194 and 195 apply to the electronic register (s 196C).
-- The Registrar's duties are encoded for what they decide and mean to the person (a member, director or secretary of a private company); there is no seat for the Registrar.
-- READING A RESULT: JUST TRUE is yes; JUST FALSE is the text's no in its own words; NOTHING is "the text does not say".
-- The core's `the day 3 January 2016` is used for the date the section names.

§ `Section 196A(1): the Registrar keeps the register`

-- src:17445 | Electronic register of members
-- src:17447 | 196A.—(1) On and after 3 January 2016, the Registrar must, in
-- src:17448 | respect of every private company, keep and maintain an electronic
-- src:17449 | register of members of that company containing such information
-- src:17450 | notified to the Registrar on or after that date.
@ref s 196A(1) (src:17445-17450)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196A(1) the Registrar must keep an electronic register of members of the company` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company is a private company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Registrar must, in respect of every private company, keep and maintain an electronic register of members" -- the text says nothing of any other company
    ELSE (IF `the date asked` LESS THAN `the day 3 January 2016`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On and after 3 January 2016, the Registrar must" (a period the text fixes in its own words; before it the periods ruling item (a) gives JUST FALSE; fork F-P5)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

DECLARE `s 196A act` IS ONE OF
    `s 196A(1) keep and maintain an electronic register of members of the private company`
    `s 196A(5) update the electronic register of members in accordance with the change`

-- The Registrar's duties have no time limit in the text: keeping the register (196A(1), MAINTENANCE) can be fulfilled or stay open, and updating it (196A(5)) takes the s 52 input, so it can end BREACH (notes/lest-without-deadline.md).
-- src:17445 | Electronic register of members
-- src:17447 | 196A.—(1) On and after 3 January 2016, the Registrar must, in
-- src:17448 | respect of every private company, keep and maintain an electronic
-- src:17449 | register of members of that company containing such information
-- src:17450 | notified to the Registrar on or after that date.
@ref s 196A(1) (src:17445-17450)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 196A act`
`s 196A(1) the Registrar must keep an electronic register of members of every private company` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 196A(1) keep and maintain an electronic register of members of the private company`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 196A(1) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not keep and maintain an electronic register of members of the private company" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: maintenance; see notes]

§ `Section 196A(2): what the electronic register contains`

DECLARE `s 196A(2) electronic register entries` HAS
    `the register contains the names of the members` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the register contains the addresses of the members that the paragraph requires` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the register contains a statement of the shares held by each member and of the amount paid or agreed to be considered as paid on the shares of each member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the register contains the date of every allotment of shares to members (including any deemed allotment as defined in section 63(3)) and the number of shares comprised in each allotment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the register contains the date on which the name of each person was entered in the register as a member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the register contains the date on which each person who ceased to be a member during the previous 7 years so ceased to be a member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the register shows every change to the information in paragraph (a)(i), (ii) and (iii) that occurs on or after 3 January 2016` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:17460 | (i) the names of the members;
@ref s 196A(2)(a)(i) (src:17460)
GIVEN entries IS A `s 196A(2) electronic register entries`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196A(2)(a)(i) the register contains the names of the members` MEANS
    IF entries's `the register contains the names of the members`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must contain (a) the following information: (i) the names of the members" (a duty not met: the provision's own question)

-- (ii): the residential address and contact address of a member who is an individual, the address of any other member.
-- src:17462 | (ii) the residential address and contact address (if the
-- src:17463 | member is an individual) or address (if otherwise) of
-- src:17464 | each member;
@ref s 196A(2)(a)(ii) (src:17462-17464)
GIVEN `the member is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the register contains the residential address of the member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the register contains the contact address of the member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the register contains the address of the member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196A(2)(a)(ii) the register contains the addresses the paragraph requires of the member` MEANS
    IF (IF `the member is an individual`
        THEN `the register contains the residential address of the member` AND `the register contains the contact address of the member`
        ELSE `the register contains the address of the member`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) the residential address and contact address (if the member is an individual) or address (if otherwise) of each member" (a duty not met)

-- src:17468 | (iii) in the case of a company having a share capital —
-- src:17470 | (A) a statement of the shares held by each member
-- src:17471 | of the amount paid or agreed to be considered
-- src:17472 | as paid on the shares of each member; and
@ref s 196A(2)(a)(iii)(A) (src:17468-17472)
GIVEN entries IS A `s 196A(2) electronic register entries`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196A(2)(a)(iii)(A) the register contains the statement of the shares and of the amount paid, for a company having a share capital` MEANS
    IF (NOT entries's `the company has a share capital`) OR entries's `the register contains a statement of the shares held by each member and of the amount paid or agreed to be considered as paid on the shares of each member`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(iii) in the case of a company having a share capital — (A) a statement of the shares held by each member of the amount paid or agreed to be considered as paid on the shares of each member" (a duty not met; a company with no share capital has nothing to state)

-- src:17468 | (iii) in the case of a company having a share capital —
-- src:17474 | (B) the date of every allotment of shares to
-- src:17475 | members (including any deemed allotment as
-- src:17476 | defined in section 63(3)) and the number of
-- src:17477 | shares comprised in each allotment;
@ref s 196A(2)(a)(iii)(B) (src:17468-17477)
GIVEN entries IS A `s 196A(2) electronic register entries`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196A(2)(a)(iii)(B) the register contains the date and size of every allotment, for a company having a share capital` MEANS
    IF (NOT entries's `the company has a share capital`) OR entries's `the register contains the date of every allotment of shares to members (including any deemed allotment as defined in section 63(3)) and the number of shares comprised in each allotment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(iii) in the case of a company having a share capital — (B) the date of every allotment of shares to members (including any deemed allotment as defined in section 63(3)) and the number of shares comprised in each allotment" (a duty not met)

-- src:17479 | (iv) the date on which the name of each person was
-- src:17480 | entered in the register as a member;
@ref s 196A(2)(a)(iv) (src:17479-17480)
GIVEN entries IS A `s 196A(2) electronic register entries`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196A(2)(a)(iv) the register contains the date on which the name of each person was entered as a member` MEANS
    IF entries's `the register contains the date on which the name of each person was entered in the register as a member`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(iv) the date on which the name of each person was entered in the register as a member" (a duty not met)

-- (v): "any person who ceased to be a member during the previous 7 years": the window of P6, from the date 7 years before the date asked up to the day before it (fork F-P6).
-- src:17482 | (v) the date on which any person who ceased to be a
-- src:17483 | member during the previous 7 years so ceased to be a
-- src:17484 | member; and
@ref s 196A(2)(a)(v) (src:17482-17484)
GIVEN `the day on which the person ceased to be a member` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 196A(2)(a)(v) the person ceased to be a member during the previous 7 years` MEANS
    `period: the date is within a period before` `the day on which the person ceased to be a member` `the date asked` 7 Years

-- src:17482 | (v) the date on which any person who ceased to be a
-- src:17483 | member during the previous 7 years so ceased to be a
-- src:17484 | member; and
@ref s 196A(2)(a)(v) (src:17482-17484)
GIVEN `the day on which the person ceased to be a member` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196A(2)(a)(v) the register must contain the date on which the person ceased to be a member` MEANS
    IF `s 196A(2)(a)(v) the person ceased to be a member during the previous 7 years` `the day on which the person ceased to be a member` `the date asked`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any person who ceased to be a member during the previous 7 years" (a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the periods ruling item (a) gives JUST FALSE; fork F-P5)

-- src:17486 | (b) any change to the information referred to in
-- src:17487 | paragraph (a)(i), (ii) and (iii) that occurs on or after
-- src:17488 | 3 January 2016.
@ref s 196A(2)(b) (src:17486-17488)
GIVEN entries IS A `s 196A(2) electronic register entries`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196A(2)(b) the register shows the changes to the information that occur on or after 3 January 2016` MEANS
    IF entries's `the register shows every change to the information in paragraph (a)(i), (ii) and (iii) that occurs on or after 3 January 2016`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) any change to the information referred to in paragraph (a)(i), (ii) and (iii) that occurs on or after 3 January 2016" (a duty not met)

-- src:17454 | (2) The electronic register of members of a private company must
-- src:17455 | be kept in such form as the Registrar may determine and must
-- src:17456 | contain —
-- src:17458 | (a) the following information:
-- src:17460 | (i) the names of the members;
-- src:17462 | (ii) the residential address and contact address (if the
-- src:17463 | member is an individual) or address (if otherwise) of
-- src:17464 | each member;
-- src:17468 | (iii) in the case of a company having a share capital —
-- src:17470 | (A) a statement of the shares held by each member
-- src:17471 | of the amount paid or agreed to be considered
-- src:17472 | as paid on the shares of each member; and
-- src:17474 | (B) the date of every allotment of shares to
-- src:17475 | members (including any deemed allotment as
-- src:17476 | defined in section 63(3)) and the number of
-- src:17477 | shares comprised in each allotment;
-- src:17479 | (iv) the date on which the name of each person was
-- src:17480 | entered in the register as a member;
-- src:17482 | (v) the date on which any person who ceased to be a
-- src:17483 | member during the previous 7 years so ceased to be a
-- src:17484 | member; and
-- src:17486 | (b) any change to the information referred to in
-- src:17487 | paragraph (a)(i), (ii) and (iii) that occurs on or after
-- src:17488 | 3 January 2016.
@ref s 196A(2) (src:17454-17488)
GIVEN entries IS A `s 196A(2) electronic register entries`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196A(2) the electronic register contains what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF     `s 196A(2)(a)(i) the register contains the names of the members` entries EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND entries's `the register contains the addresses of the members that the paragraph requires`
       AND `s 196A(2)(a)(iii)(A) the register contains the statement of the shares and of the amount paid, for a company having a share capital` entries EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `s 196A(2)(a)(iii)(B) the register contains the date and size of every allotment, for a company having a share capital` entries EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `s 196A(2)(a)(iv) the register contains the date on which the name of each person was entered as a member` entries EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND entries's `the register contains the date on which each person who ceased to be a member during the previous 7 years so ceased to be a member`
       AND `s 196A(2)(b) the register shows the changes to the information that occur on or after 3 January 2016` entries EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The electronic register of members of a private company must be kept in such form as the Registrar may determine and must contain (a) the following information ...; and (b) any change ..." (a duty not met: the provision's own question)

§ `Section 196A(3) to (6): stock, changes, updating and evidence`

-- src:17495 | (3) Where a private company has converted any of its shares into
-- src:17496 | stock and the company notifies the Registrar of this fact, the register
-- src:17497 | must show the amount of stock or number of stock units held by each
-- src:17498 | member instead of the number of shares and the particulars relating to
-- src:17499 | shares specified in subsection (2)(a).
@ref s 196A(3) (src:17495-17499)
GIVEN `the private company has converted any of its shares into stock` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company notifies the Registrar of the conversion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196A(3) the electronic register must show stock instead of shares` MEANS
    IF `the private company has converted any of its shares into stock` AND `the company notifies the Registrar of the conversion`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a private company has converted any of its shares into stock and the company notifies the Registrar of this fact, the register must show the amount of stock or number of stock units held by each member instead of the number of shares" (a duty gated by "Where"; the periods ruling item (b); fork F-W1)

-- src:17503 | (4) Particulars of any change in the information referred to in
-- src:17504 | subsection (2) must be given to the Registrar where a private
-- src:17505 | company purchases one or more of its shares or stocks in
-- src:17506 | circumstances in which section 76H applies unless the company
-- src:17507 | cancels all the shares or stocks immediately after the purchase in
-- src:17508 | accordance with section 76K(1).
@ref s 196A(4) (src:17503-17508)
GIVEN `the private company purchases one or more of its shares or stocks in circumstances in which section 76H applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company cancels all the shares or stocks immediately after the purchase in accordance with section 76K(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196A(4) particulars of the change must be given to the Registrar` MEANS
    IF `the private company purchases one or more of its shares or stocks in circumstances in which section 76H applies`
    THEN (IF `the company cancels all the shares or stocks immediately after the purchase in accordance with section 76K(1)`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be given to the Registrar where a private company purchases ... unless the company cancels all the shares or stocks immediately after the purchase" ("unless" met)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a private company purchases one or more of its shares or stocks in circumstances in which section 76H applies" (the "where" gate unmet; fork F-W1). The text names no bearer of the duty, so there is no regulative rule (fork F-B1).

-- src:17512 | (5) The Registrar must update the electronic register of members in
-- src:17513 | accordance with any change that is required or authorised by any
-- src:17514 | provision of this Act to be lodged with the Registrar, including
-- src:17515 | section 31(1), 63(1), 70(6), 71(1B), 74A(3), 76B(7), 76K(1A), 126(2)
-- src:17516 | or 128(1)(a).
@ref s 196A(5) (src:17512-17516)
GIVEN `the change is lodged under section 31(1), 63(1), 70(6), 71(1B), 74A(3), 76B(7), 76K(1A), 126(2) or 128(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the change is required or authorised by another provision of this Act to be lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196A(5) the Registrar must update the electronic register of members in accordance with the change` MEANS
    IF `the change is lodged under section 31(1), 63(1), 70(6), 71(1B), 74A(3), 76B(7), 76K(1A), 126(2) or 128(1)(a)` OR `the change is required or authorised by another provision of this Act to be lodged with the Registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "any change that is required or authorised by any provision of this Act to be lodged with the Registrar, including section 31(1), ..." (a list the text opens with "including"); the text is silent on a change lodged under no provision

-- src:17512 | (5) The Registrar must update the electronic register of members in
-- src:17513 | accordance with any change that is required or authorised by any
-- src:17514 | provision of this Act to be lodged with the Registrar, including
-- src:17515 | section 31(1), 63(1), 70(6), 71(1B), 74A(3), 76B(7), 76K(1A), 126(2)
-- src:17516 | or 128(1)(a).
@ref s 196A(5) (src:17512-17516)
GIVEN `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 196A act`
`s 196A(5) the Registrar must update the electronic register of members` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 196A(5) update the electronic register of members in accordance with the change`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not update the electronic register of members in accordance with the change"

-- src:17520 | (6) An entry in the register of members required to be kept by the
-- src:17521 | Registrar under this section is prima facie evidence of the truth of any
-- src:17522 | matters which are by this Act directed or authorised to be entered or
-- src:17523 | inserted in the register of members.
@ref s 196A(6) (src:17520-17523)
GIVEN `the entry is in the electronic register of members required to be kept by the Registrar under section 196A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is directed or authorised by this Act to be entered or inserted in the register of members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196A(6) the entry is prima facie evidence of the truth of the matter` MEANS
    IF `the entry is in the electronic register of members required to be kept by the Registrar under section 196A` AND `the matter is directed or authorised by this Act to be entered or inserted in the register of members`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An entry in the register ... is prima facie evidence of the truth of any matters which are by this Act directed or authorised to be entered or inserted" -- the text speaks of those matters and is silent on any other

§ `Section 196B: information from private companies that existed before 3 January 2016`

-- src:17529 | 196B.—(1) A private company incorporated, or converted from a
-- src:17530 | public company, before 3 January 2016 must lodge with the Registrar
-- src:17531 | the information necessary to be included in the company’s electronic
-- src:17532 | register of members under section 196A within the earlier of the
-- src:17533 | following dates:
@ref s 196B(1) (src:17529-17533)
GIVEN `the private company was incorporated, or converted from a public company, before 3 January 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196B(1) the private company must lodge the information with the Registrar` MEANS
    IF `the private company was incorporated, or converted from a public company, before 3 January 2016`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A private company incorporated, or converted from a public company, before 3 January 2016 must lodge" -- the text says nothing of a company incorporated or converted on or after that date (no "only")

-- (a) 6 months after 3 January 2016; (b) the date on which the first return under section 197 is required to be lodged after 3 January 2016 (supplied: it is the last day for that return, s 197); the earlier governs.
-- src:17535 | (a) 6 months after 3 January 2016;
@ref s 196B(1)(a) (src:17535)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 196B(1)(a) the date 6 months after 3 January 2016` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day 3 January 2016` 6 Months

-- src:17529 | 196B.—(1) A private company incorporated, or converted from a
-- src:17530 | public company, before 3 January 2016 must lodge with the Registrar
-- src:17531 | the information necessary to be included in the company’s electronic
-- src:17532 | register of members under section 196A within the earlier of the
-- src:17533 | following dates:
-- src:17535 | (a) 6 months after 3 January 2016;
-- src:17537 | (b) the date on which the first return under section 197 is
-- src:17538 | required to be lodged with the Registrar after 3 January
-- src:17539 | 2016.
@ref s 196B(1) (src:17529-17539)
GIVEN `the date on which the first return under section 197 is required to be lodged with the Registrar after 3 January 2016` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 196B(1) the last day for lodging the information` MEANS
    IF `s 196B(1)(a) the date 6 months after 3 January 2016` LESS THAN `the date on which the first return under section 197 is required to be lodged with the Registrar after 3 January 2016`
    THEN `s 196B(1)(a) the date 6 months after 3 January 2016`
    ELSE `the date on which the first return under section 197 is required to be lodged with the Registrar after 3 January 2016`

-- src:17529 | 196B.—(1) A private company incorporated, or converted from a
-- src:17530 | public company, before 3 January 2016 must lodge with the Registrar
-- src:17531 | the information necessary to be included in the company’s electronic
-- src:17532 | register of members under section 196A within the earlier of the
-- src:17533 | following dates:
-- src:17535 | (a) 6 months after 3 January 2016;
-- src:17537 | (b) the date on which the first return under section 197 is
-- src:17538 | required to be lodged with the Registrar after 3 January
-- src:17539 | 2016.
@ref s 196B(1) (src:17529-17539)
GIVEN `the date on which the first return under section 197 is required to be lodged with the Registrar after 3 January 2016` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the information is lodged with the Registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 196B(1) the information was lodged by the last day` MEANS
    `the day on which the information is lodged with the Registrar` AT MOST `s 196B(1) the last day for lodging the information` `the date on which the first return under section 197 is required to be lodged with the Registrar after 3 January 2016`

DECLARE `s 196B act` IS ONE OF
    `s 196B(1) lodge with the Registrar the information necessary to be included in the electronic register of members`

-- The trace clock counts days after 3 January 2016 (AT 0).
-- src:17529 | 196B.—(1) A private company incorporated, or converted from a
-- src:17530 | public company, before 3 January 2016 must lodge with the Registrar
-- src:17531 | the information necessary to be included in the company’s electronic
-- src:17532 | register of members under section 196A within the earlier of the
-- src:17533 | following dates:
-- src:17535 | (a) 6 months after 3 January 2016;
-- src:17537 | (b) the date on which the first return under section 197 is
-- src:17538 | required to be lodged with the Registrar after 3 January
-- src:17539 | 2016.
@ref s 196B(1) (src:17529-17539)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the date on which the first return under section 197 is required to be lodged with the Registrar after 3 January 2016` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 196B act`
`s 196B(1) a private company must lodge the information by the earlier of the two dates` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 196B(1) lodge with the Registrar the information necessary to be included in the electronic register of members`
    WITHIN `s 196B(1) the last day for lodging the information` `the date on which the first return under section 197 is required to be lodged with the Registrar after 3 January 2016` MINUS `the day 3 January 2016`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the private company did not lodge the information for the electronic register of members by the earlier of the two dates in section 196B(1)"

-- src:17546 | (2) If a private company to which subsection (1) applies fails to
-- src:17547 | lodge any of the information that it is required to lodge under that
-- src:17548 | subsection, the Registrar may, in place of the omitted information,
-- src:17549 | enter in the electronic register of members the corresponding
-- src:17550 | information contained in the register of members kept by the
-- src:17551 | company under section 190 in force immediately before 3 January
-- src:17552 | 2016.
@ref s 196B(2) (src:17546-17552)
GIVEN `the private company is one to which section 196B(1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company fails to lodge any of the information that it is required to lodge under section 196B(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196B(2) the Registrar may enter the corresponding information from the old register of members` MEANS
    IF `the private company is one to which section 196B(1) applies` AND `the company fails to lodge any of the information that it is required to lodge under section 196B(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a private company to which subsection (1) applies fails to lodge any of the information ..., the Registrar may, in place of the omitted information, enter" (a power whose "If" gate failed; the grant ruling, limit 1; fork F-G1)

-- src:17556 | (3) The Registrar may extend the time for furnishing the
-- src:17557 | information under subsection (1) if the Registrar considers it fair
-- src:17558 | and reasonable to do so in the circumstances of the case.
@ref s 196B(3) (src:17556-17558)
GIVEN `the Registrar considers it fair and reasonable to extend the time in the circumstances of the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196B(3) the Registrar may extend the time for furnishing the information` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar considers it fair and reasonable to extend the time in the circumstances of the case`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Registrar may extend the time ... if the Registrar considers it fair and reasonable to do so" (a power whose "if" gate failed; the grant ruling, limit 1; fork F-G1; the judgment is the Registrar's, taken as a fact)

§ `Section 196C: sections 194 and 195 apply to the electronic register`

-- src:17564 | 196C.—(1) Section 194 applies in respect of the electronic register
-- src:17565 | of members of a private company required to be kept by the Registrar
-- src:17566 | under section 196A as if a reference to a register under section 194
-- src:17567 | referred to the electronic register of members of the private company
-- src:17568 | in question.
@ref s 196C(1) (src:17564-17568)
GIVEN `the register is the electronic register of members of a private company required to be kept by the Registrar under section 196A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196C(1) section 194 applies in respect of the electronic register of members` MEANS
    IF `the register is the electronic register of members of a private company required to be kept by the Registrar under section 196A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Section 194 applies in respect of the electronic register of members of a private company required to be kept by the Registrar under section 196A" -- the text says nothing of any other register

-- src:17572 | (2) Section 195 applies in respect of the electronic register of
-- src:17573 | members of a private company required to be kept by the Registrar
-- src:17574 | under section 196A but with the following modifications:
@ref s 196C(2) (src:17572-17574)
GIVEN `the register is the electronic register of members of a private company required to be kept by the Registrar under section 196A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196C(2) section 195 applies in respect of the electronic register of members, with the modifications` MEANS
    IF `the register is the electronic register of members of a private company required to be kept by the Registrar under section 196A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Section 195 applies in respect of the electronic register of members of a private company required to be kept by the Registrar under section 196A but with the following modifications" -- the text says nothing of any other register

DECLARE `s 196C(2) reference in section 195` IS ONE OF
    `s 196C(2) a reference to a register under section 194`
    `s 196C(2) a reference to a branch register`
    `s 196C(2) some other reference`

-- (a): "a reference to a register under section 194 refers to the electronic register of members of the private company in question". The rendering says "under section 194" in a paragraph that modifies section 195 (finding 2 in NOTES.md); the text is followed as printed.
-- src:17576 | (a) a reference to a register under section 194 refers to the
-- src:17577 | electronic register of members of the private company in
-- src:17578 | question;
@ref s 196C(2)(a) (src:17576-17578)
GIVEN reference IS A `s 196C(2) reference in section 195`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196C(2)(a) the reference is read as a reference to the electronic register of the private company` MEANS
    CONSIDER reference
    WHEN `s 196C(2) a reference to a register under section 194` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (a) modifies "a reference to a register under section 194" and says nothing of any other reference

-- (b): "the reference to any branch register were omitted".
-- src:17580 | (b) the reference to any branch register were omitted;
@ref s 196C(2)(b) (src:17580)
GIVEN reference IS A `s 196C(2) reference in section 195`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196C(2)(b) the reference is omitted` MEANS
    CONSIDER reference
    WHEN `s 196C(2) a reference to a branch register` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (b) omits "the reference to any branch register" and says nothing of any other reference

-- src:17582 | (c) the company is required to notify the Registrar of any
-- src:17583 | request made by a trustee under section 195(3) for the
-- src:17584 | relevant shares to be marked in the electronic register of
-- src:17585 | members as to identify the shares being held in respect of a
-- src:17586 | trust within 14 days after the request.
@ref s 196C(2)(c) (src:17582-17586)
GIVEN `the trustee has made a request under section 195(3) for the relevant shares to be marked in the electronic register of members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196C(2)(c) the company must notify the Registrar of the trustee's request` MEANS
    IF `the trustee has made a request under section 195(3) for the relevant shares to be marked in the electronic register of members`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the duty is "to notify the Registrar of any request made by a trustee under section 195(3)"; without a request the text says nothing (fork F-E1)

-- src:17582 | (c) the company is required to notify the Registrar of any
-- src:17583 | request made by a trustee under section 195(3) for the
-- src:17584 | relevant shares to be marked in the electronic register of
-- src:17585 | members as to identify the shares being held in respect of a
-- src:17586 | trust within 14 days after the request.
@ref s 196C(2)(c) (src:17582-17586)
GIVEN `the day on which the trustee makes the request` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 196C(2)(c) the last day for notifying the Registrar` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day on which the trustee makes the request` 14 Days

-- src:17582 | (c) the company is required to notify the Registrar of any
-- src:17583 | request made by a trustee under section 195(3) for the
-- src:17584 | relevant shares to be marked in the electronic register of
-- src:17585 | members as to identify the shares being held in respect of a
-- src:17586 | trust within 14 days after the request.
@ref s 196C(2)(c) (src:17582-17586)
GIVEN `the day on which the trustee makes the request` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the company notifies the Registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 196C(2)(c) the Registrar was notified within 14 days after the request` MEANS
    `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day on which the trustee makes the request` `the day on which the company notifies the Registrar` 14 Days

DECLARE `s 196C act` IS ONE OF
    `s 196C(2)(c) notify the Registrar of the trustee's request that the relevant shares be marked`

-- src:17582 | (c) the company is required to notify the Registrar of any
-- src:17583 | request made by a trustee under section 195(3) for the
-- src:17584 | relevant shares to be marked in the electronic register of
-- src:17585 | members as to identify the shares being held in respect of a
-- src:17586 | trust within 14 days after the request.
@ref s 196C(2)(c) (src:17582-17586)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 196C act`
`s 196C(2)(c) a private company must notify the Registrar of the trustee's request within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 196C(2)(c) notify the Registrar of the trustee's request that the relevant shares be marked`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the private company did not notify the Registrar of the trustee's request within 14 days after the request"

§ `Section 196D: the old register of members`

-- src:17595 | 196D.—(1) Subject to subsections (2) and (3), a private company
-- src:17596 | incorporated, or which was converted from a public company before
-- src:17597 | 3 January 2016 must —
@ref s 196D(1) (src:17595-17597)
GIVEN `the private company was incorporated, or converted from a public company, before 3 January 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196D(1) the private company must keep its old registers` MEANS
    IF `the private company was incorporated, or converted from a public company, before 3 January 2016`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a private company incorporated, or which was converted from a public company before 3 January 2016 must" -- the text says nothing of a company incorporated or converted on or after that date (no "only")

-- (a): the branch register in force immediately before 3 January 2016, for 7 years after that date.
-- src:17599 | (a) continue to keep any branch register of members under
-- src:17600 | section 196 in force immediately before 3 January 2016 for
-- src:17601 | a period of 7 years after that date; and
@ref s 196D(1)(a) (src:17599-17601)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 196D(1)(a) the last day of the period for keeping the branch register` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day 3 January 2016` 7 Years

-- src:17599 | (a) continue to keep any branch register of members under
-- src:17600 | section 196 in force immediately before 3 January 2016 for
-- src:17601 | a period of 7 years after that date; and
@ref s 196D(1)(a) (src:17599-17601)
GIVEN `the company kept a branch register of members under section 196 in force immediately before 3 January 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196D(1)(a) the private company must continue to keep the branch register` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company kept a branch register of members under section 196 in force immediately before 3 January 2016`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "continue to keep any branch register of members under section 196 in force immediately before 3 January 2016" -- no such register, no duty stated
    ELSE (IF     `the date asked` AT LEAST `the day 3 January 2016`
             AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day 3 January 2016` `the date asked` 7 Years
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period of 7 years after that date" (a period the text fixes in its own words; before and after it the periods ruling item (a) gives JUST FALSE; fork F-P5; the edges are those of F-P2: the day of the event is in, the last day is in)

-- (b): the register of members under section 190(1) in force immediately before 3 January 2016, for 7 years after the last member referred to in it ceases to be a member.
-- src:17603 | (b) continue to keep its register of members under
-- src:17604 | section 190(1) in force immediately before 3 January
-- src:17605 | 2016 for a period of 7 years after the last member referred
-- src:17606 | to in the register ceases to be a member of the company.
@ref s 196D(1)(b) (src:17603-17606)
GIVEN `the day on which the last member referred to in the register ceased to be a member of the company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 196D(1)(b) the last day of the period for keeping the register of members` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day on which the last member referred to in the register ceased to be a member of the company` 7 Years

-- src:17603 | (b) continue to keep its register of members under
-- src:17604 | section 190(1) in force immediately before 3 January
-- src:17605 | 2016 for a period of 7 years after the last member referred
-- src:17606 | to in the register ceases to be a member of the company.
@ref s 196D(1)(b) (src:17603-17606)
GIVEN `the company kept a register of members under section 190(1) in force immediately before 3 January 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
      `every member referred to in the register has ceased to be a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the last member referred to in the register ceased to be a member of the company` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196D(1)(b) the private company must continue to keep its register of members` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company kept a register of members under section 190(1) in force immediately before 3 January 2016`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "continue to keep its register of members under section 190(1) in force immediately before 3 January 2016" -- no such register, no duty stated
    ELSE (IF (NOT `every member referred to in the register has ceased to be a member of the company`) OR `the date asked` LESS THAN `the day on which the last member referred to in the register ceased to be a member of the company`
          THEN JUST TRUE   -- the 7 years run "after the last member referred to in the register ceases to be a member", so they have not begun and the register is still to be kept
          ELSE (IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day on which the last member referred to in the register ceased to be a member of the company` `the date asked` 7 Years
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period of 7 years after the last member referred to in the register ceases to be a member of the company" (a period the text fixes in its own words; fork F-P5; the edges are those of F-P2)

DECLARE `s 196D act` IS ONE OF
    `s 196D(1)(a) stop keeping the branch register`
    `s 196D(1)(b) stop keeping the register of members`

-- "must continue to keep ... for a period of 7 years": read as a prohibition on stopping within the period (the derived SHANT of the N2 ruling).
-- The trace clock counts days after 3 January 2016 (AT 0); the period ends 2,557 days later (3 January 2023).
-- src:17595 | 196D.—(1) Subject to subsections (2) and (3), a private company
-- src:17596 | incorporated, or which was converted from a public company before
-- src:17597 | 3 January 2016 must —
-- src:17599 | (a) continue to keep any branch register of members under
-- src:17600 | section 196 in force immediately before 3 January 2016 for
-- src:17601 | a period of 7 years after that date; and
@ref s 196D(1)(a) (src:17595-17601)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 196D act`
`s 196D(1)(a) a private company must not stop keeping the branch register within 7 years after 3 January 2016` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    SHANT `s 196D(1)(a) stop keeping the branch register`
    WITHIN `s 196D(1)(a) the last day of the period for keeping the branch register` MINUS `the day 3 January 2016`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the private company stopped keeping its branch register within 7 years after 3 January 2016"

-- src:17595 | 196D.—(1) Subject to subsections (2) and (3), a private company
-- src:17596 | incorporated, or which was converted from a public company before
-- src:17597 | 3 January 2016 must —
-- src:17603 | (b) continue to keep its register of members under
-- src:17604 | section 190(1) in force immediately before 3 January
-- src:17605 | 2016 for a period of 7 years after the last member referred
-- src:17606 | to in the register ceases to be a member of the company.
@ref s 196D(1)(b) (src:17595-17606)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the day on which the last member referred to in the register ceased to be a member of the company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 196D act`
`s 196D(1)(b) a private company must not stop keeping its register of members within 7 years after the last member ceased` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    SHANT `s 196D(1)(b) stop keeping the register of members`
    WITHIN `s 196D(1)(b) the last day of the period for keeping the register of members` `the day on which the last member referred to in the register ceased to be a member of the company` MINUS `the day on which the last member referred to in the register ceased to be a member of the company`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the private company stopped keeping its register of members within 7 years after the last member referred to in it ceased to be a member"

-- src:17610 | (2) A private company is not required to update the branch register
-- src:17611 | or the register of members required to be kept under subsection (1)
-- src:17612 | with any changes in the particulars therein that occurred on or after
-- src:17613 | the date on which the company furnishes the information required to
-- src:17614 | be furnished to the Registrar under section 196B(1).
@ref s 196D(2) (src:17610-17614)
GIVEN `the day of the change in the particulars` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the company furnishes the information required to be furnished to the Registrar under section 196B(1)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196D(2) the private company is not required to update the old register for the change` MEANS
    IF `the day of the change in the particulars` AT LEAST `the day on which the company furnishes the information required to be furnished to the Registrar under section 196B(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "not required to update ... with any changes in the particulars therein that occurred on or after the date on which the company furnishes the information" -- an earlier change is outside the exemption, and the text does not say it must be entered

-- src:17618 | (3) Until the expiry of the period for which any branch register and
-- src:17619 | register of members is required to be kept under subsection (1) but
-- src:17620 | subject to subsection (2) —
-- src:17622 | (a) sections 190, 191, 192(2), (3) and (4), 194, 195 and 196 in
-- src:17623 | force immediately before 3 January 2016 continue, with
-- src:17624 | the necessary modifications, to apply in relation to the
-- src:17625 | branch register and register of members required to be kept
-- src:17626 | under subsection (1); and
@ref s 196D(3)(a) (src:17618-17626)
GIVEN `the date asked is within the period for which the old register is required to be kept under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196D(3)(a) the old sections continue to apply to the old registers` MEANS
    IF `the date asked is within the period for which the old register is required to be kept under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Until the expiry of the period for which any branch register and register of members is required to be kept under subsection (1) ... sections 190, 191, 192(2), (3) and (4), 194, 195 and 196 in force immediately before 3 January 2016 continue, with the necessary modifications, to apply" ("Until": after the expiry the text's no; the old sections themselves are not among the sources)

-- src:17618 | (3) Until the expiry of the period for which any branch register and
-- src:17619 | register of members is required to be kept under subsection (1) but
-- src:17620 | subject to subsection (2) —
-- src:17628 | (b) any non‑compliance with the sections mentioned in
-- src:17629 | paragraph (a) may be dealt with and punished in
-- src:17630 | accordance with those provisions as if they were in force
-- src:17631 | immediately before 3 January 2016.
@ref s 196D(3)(b) (src:17618-17631)
GIVEN `the date asked is within the period for which the old register is required to be kept under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the non-compliance is with a section mentioned in paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196D(3)(b) the non-compliance may be dealt with and punished as if the old sections were in force` MEANS
    IF NOT `the date asked is within the period for which the old register is required to be kept under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Until the expiry of the period for which any branch register and register of members is required to be kept under subsection (1) ... any non-compliance ... may be dealt with and punished" ("Until": after the expiry the periods ruling item (a) and the "In short" line on "until" give JUST FALSE; fork F-P5)
    ELSE (IF `the non-compliance is with a section mentioned in paragraph (a)`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any non-compliance with the sections mentioned in paragraph (a) may be dealt with and punished in accordance with those provisions as if they were in force immediately before 3 January 2016" (a grant limited to those sections; the grant ruling, limit 1)

§ `Section 196E: the address of an individual member`

-- src:17641 | 196E. As from the date of commencement of section 43 of the
-- src:17642 | ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024, the
-- src:17643 | Registrar must cause —
-- src:17645 | (a) the address contained in the electronic register of members
-- src:17646 | of each member who is an individual to be kept as the
-- src:17647 | residential address of that member and, until notice of a
-- src:17648 | change in the individual’s contact address is lodged under
-- src:17649 | any ACRA administered Act on or after that date, also as
-- src:17650 | the contact address of that member; and
@ref s 196E(a) (src:17641-17650)
GIVEN `the member is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of commencement of section 43 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196E(a) the address in the electronic register is kept as the residential address of the member` MEANS
    IF NOT `the member is an individual`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "each member who is an individual" -- the text says nothing of another member
    ELSE (IF `the date asked` AT LEAST `the date of commencement of section 43 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "As from the date of commencement of section 43 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024, the Registrar must cause" (a period the text fixes in its own words; before it the periods ruling item (a) gives JUST FALSE; fork F-P5)

-- src:17641 | 196E. As from the date of commencement of section 43 of the
-- src:17642 | ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024, the
-- src:17643 | Registrar must cause —
-- src:17645 | (a) the address contained in the electronic register of members
-- src:17646 | of each member who is an individual to be kept as the
-- src:17647 | residential address of that member and, until notice of a
-- src:17648 | change in the individual’s contact address is lodged under
-- src:17649 | any ACRA administered Act on or after that date, also as
-- src:17650 | the contact address of that member; and
@ref s 196E(a) (src:17641-17650)
GIVEN `the member is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of commencement of section 43 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024` IS A DATE
      `a notice of a change in the individual's contact address has been lodged under any ACRA administered Act on or after that date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196E(a) the address in the electronic register is also kept as the contact address of the member` MEANS
    IF NOT `the member is an individual`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "each member who is an individual" -- the text says nothing of another member
    ELSE (IF `the date asked` LESS THAN `the date of commencement of section 43 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "As from the date of commencement" (before it; fork F-P5)
          ELSE (IF `a notice of a change in the individual's contact address has been lodged under any ACRA administered Act on or after that date`
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until notice of a change in the individual's contact address is lodged under any ACRA administered Act on or after that date, also as the contact address" ("until" met)
                ELSE JUST TRUE))

-- src:17652 | (b) that contact address to be made available for public access
-- src:17653 | under section 12(2)(d) as the address of that member.
@ref s 196E(b) (src:17652-17653)
GIVEN `the member is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of commencement of section 43 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 196E(b) the contact address is made available for public access under section 12(2)(d) as the address of the member` MEANS
    IF NOT `the member is an individual`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the address of that member" is stated for "each member who is an individual"
    ELSE (IF `the date asked` AT LEAST `the date of commencement of section 43 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "As from the date of commencement of section 43 ..., the Registrar must cause (b) that contact address to be made available for public access under section 12(2)(d)" (before the commencement; fork F-P5)
